# Known bug: a spell cast without paying its mana cost still announces X (actions.rs `x_symbols` ignores `instead`), so Walking Ballista
# cast free is given X = 1 when the player asks for it and pays {1}{1} from the pool; CR 107.3b says X is 0.
#
# CR 107.3b: if a spell is cast without paying its mana cost, X is 0. Mind's Desire exiles the top card of a library of Walking
# Ballistas (so the shuffle cannot matter) for each of its copies, and Bot1 may cast one free until end of turn. Two mana float
# unspent in Bot1's pool from the extra Moxen, so it could pay X = 1 ({X}{X}) if X were announced; it is not, the Ballista
# enters with no +1/+1 counters, is a 0/0, and dies (CR 704.5f).

